Package: sampleid
Type: Package
Title: Biological Sample Identifier Management and Validation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gbèna Ulrich Evrard", "Lokonon",
           email = "ulrichlokn@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a collection of tools for the systematic
    management, standardization, validation, and harmonization of
    biological sample identifiers across datasets and research
    workflows. Designed for applications in genomics, metagenomics,
    metatranscriptomics, transcriptomics, and other data-intensive
    biological disciplines, the package supports identifier
    normalization, duplicate identification, collision detection,
    sample matching, consistency assessment, cross-dataset
    comparison, and sample reconciliation. Additional utilities
    facilitate sample table import, data integrity assessment,
    and quality reporting. By helping detect identifier
    inconsistencies and potential sample misidentification,
    sampleid aims to strengthen data integrity, traceability,
    interoperability, and reproducibility in biological research.
